<article class="env-definition" id="0C47">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C47">Definition <span data-tag="0C47">53.19.1</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a $1$-dimensional locally algebraic $k$-scheme. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say a closed point $x \in X$ is a <em>node</em>, or an <em>ordinary double point</em>, or <em>defines a nodal singularity</em> if there exists an ordinary double point $\overline{x} \in X_{\overline{k}}$ mapping to $x$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say the <em>singularities of $X$ are at-worst-nodal</em> if all closed points of $X$ are either in the smooth locus of the structure morphism $X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ or are ordinary double points. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>